# The rest of the phases a script can reach: the world map, a location's narration, the management
# screen and the settings screen. Companion to pause_early_phases.cli — see its header for why this
# is worth a test at all.
#
# Settings is the second gap this found: its only exit is one small Back button, and Escape was not
# handled there, which on a screen with nothing else on it reads as a freeze.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --silent --no-save --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Yard" --period noon

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue

# ── World map ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
wait mode WorldView 60
pause
wait mode MainMenu 20

# ── Settings ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Opened from the menu, and Escape is the same press as its Back button.
click menu Settings
wait mode Settings 20
pause
wait mode MainMenu 20

click menu Continue
wait mode WorldView 20

# ── Narration ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The menu opens as an OVERLAY: narration is not torn down, and Continue resumes the same scene.
# Leaving a location is the footer LEAVE button's job, not Escape's.
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
pause
wait mode MainMenu 20
click menu Continue
wait mode LocationInteraction 30

# ── Management ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Opened over narration, and Escape closes it back to the menu rather than to the scene.
manage
wait mode ProtagonistManagement 20
pause
wait mode MainMenu 20
click menu Continue
wait mode LocationInteraction 30

quit
